  "title": "The Lift to Floor Seven",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "mechanical puzzles",
  "premise": "A toy lift starts at floor 0 and must reach floor 7 using a +3 button and a -2 button, without leaving floors 0 through 9. The operator tries four moves in the order +3, +3, -2, +3, yielding 0, 3, 6, 4, 7; the lift opens to a tiny rooftop garden.",
  "hook": "Up three. Down two. Can we land on seven?",
  "visible_action": "Floor display changes 0 to 3 to 6 to 4 to 7; an on-screen path traces four presses; garden panels unfold.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Write the actual sequence before calling a route impossible.",
  "gate": "Verified four-press route. Equation 3u-2d=7 has shortest nonnegative solution u=3,d=1; all listed floors stay within bounds.",
